 adjustment joystick by pushing it to the  left or right depending on the direction  she wants to go no she wants to go left  so she presses left words  trailer assists relies on many  components that are already present Park  Assist power steering electric mirror  adjustment the rear-view camera and the  infotainment display all of these  components work together to prevent the  trailer from suddenly ending up in the  wrong place  Sophie says that at first it was a bit  strange to steer the car and the tree  there using just the little mirror  adjustment button but once you've done  it a few times it's relatively easy  especially because you can see the  direction you're going on this  infotainment display here Rhino says the  good news is trailer Assist works  straightaway the bad news is it costs  extra and you need to combine components  to make it work for instance the  rear-view camera and the trailer hitch  with the electrical installation kit the  system cost nine hundred thirty five  euros and the trailer hitch another  eight hundred eighty but trailer assist  does give drivers a sense of security so  they can relax when they're pulling a  big load even in tight spaces or  situations with poor visibility backing  up is no longer a problem
 

